li  president touched on geopolitics at uh  towards the end of his speech he  referred to iran's nuclear ambitions  what do you say about that indeed he did  and he basically did derive a german  responsibility uh from the crimes of the  holocaust also in regard to stopping  iran  as he said he said iran is dedicated to  israel's destruction he said that same  thing by the way when he met  german president steinmeier on sunday  and that the accord currently being  negotiated by germany and other powers  to try to get iran to return to the 2015  nuclear deal  he said on sunday uh in somewhat more  direct uh speech is toothless and  watered down and that it must be stopped  somewhat more diplomatically he uh  indicated the same here to the bundestag  today  a very important moment in german  israeli relations right now we've seen a  compensation agreement for the victims  of the munich olympics massacre finally  agreed after so long what does all this  say about german israeli relations right  now melinda well the reason that we're  hearing not only the two speakers today  stress the duty to remember and the  special responsibility that germany has  to israel but also yesterday at the  commemoration in munich at the airfield  where the israeli hostages most of them  were killed two were killed in the  olympic village of course but the reason  we're hearing this stressed so  forcefully by all of the speakers is  that in fact we are seeing a divergence  in german and israeli attitudes when it  comes to exactly this point with the  majority of israel israelis saying this  is an ongoing responsibility that  germany has for the jewish people and  for the israeli state whereas a minority  of germans see it that way and in fact  nearly half of germans say it's time to  draw a line under history that  will be regarded by many many uh people  including within the german political  leadership with alarm as will a further  finding of a recent study that fully a  quarter of germans say that jews have  too much power in the world an  anti-semitic trope that clearly is being  fomented by social media by hate site  sites hate speech sites and that's one  reason we heard the president of the  bundestag today emphasizing the  importance of political leadership to  fight ingrained anti-semitism which she  said is at the heart  of german political culture or german  culture in many ways  melinda thank you so much our chief  political correspondent melinda crane  you
 

